%N A400904 Decimal expansion of -Sum_{n>=1} mu(n)*(n^(1/n) - 1), where mu is the Moebius function.
%C A400904 The Moebius analog of the MRB constant A037077 (which is Sum_{n>=1} (-1)^n*(n^(1/n) - 1)).
%C A400904 The series converges (conditionally): writing n^(1/n) - 1 = log(n)/n + r(n) with Sum |r(n)| < oo, convergence follows from the prime number theorem in the form Sum_{n>=1} mu(n)*log(n)/n = -1.
%C A400904 Partial sums converge very slowly (the sum over n <= 2*10^7 is correct to only about 2 decimal places); the formula below converges geometrically.
%F A400904 Equals 1 - Sum_{k>=2} ((-1)^k/k!) * (d^k/ds^k) (1/zeta(s)) at s = k.
%F A400904 Equals 1 - Sum_{n>=1} mu(n)*(n^(1/n) - 1 - log(n)/n).
%e A400904 1.191446361317200377067868241829807247386620785499968888911365829647669819954408821117690285...
%o A400904 (PARI) \p 130
%o A400904 S(k) = k + x + O(x^(k+1));
%o A400904 -(-1 + sum(k = 2, 80, (-1)^k * polcoef(1/zeta(S(k)), k)))
%Y A400904 Cf. A008683, A037077, A363704.
%K A400904 nonn,cons
%O A400904 1,3
